T:What it is
T:Navigation
T:is a field
T:of study
T:that focuses
T:on the
T:process of
T:monitoring
T:and
T:controlling
T:the movement
T:of a craft
T:or vehicle
T:from one
T:place to
T:another. The
T:field of
T:navigation
T:includes
T:four general
T:categories:
T:land
T:navigation,
T:marine
T:navigation,
T:aeronautic
T:navigation,
T:and space
T:navigation.
T:It is also
T:the term of
T:art used for
T:the
T:specialized
T:knowledge
T:used by
T:navigators
T:to perform
T:navigation
T:tasks. All
T:navigational
T:techniques
T:involve
T:locating the
T:navigator's
T:position
T:compared to
T:known
T:locations or
T:patterns.
T:Navigation,
T:in a broader
T:sense, can
T:refer to any
T:skill or
T:study that
T:involves the
T:determinatio
T:of position
T:and
T:direction.
T:In this
T:sense,
T:navigation
T:includes
T:orienteering
T:and
T:pedestrian
T:navigation.
